<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 240 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 240 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 240 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>		EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    500 MLN!   =	    779 MLN!  1.019 BLN!</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS     =	   =	    123 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS     =	   =	    156 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE     =		=	  240 MLN</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 500 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING IN EQUAL AMOUNTS ON 4 &amp; 5</p>
<p>MARCH AT 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE 5-15/16 PERCENT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
